 "title": "Auditors &amp; Welfare Office - Oglala Lakota County, South Dakota",
 "text": "Auditors & Welfare Office - Oglala Lakota County, South Dakota\nSkip to content\nOctober 18, 2026\nOglala Lakota County, South Dakota\nHome\nOnline Map\nAbout\nDirectory »\nAuditors & Welfare Office\nClerk of Court\nPublic Health Nurse\nDirector of Equalization\nEmergency Management\nGIS\nHighway Department\nPlanning & Zoning\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nState’s Attorney\nTreasurer\nVeterans Service Officer\nWeed & Pest\nCommission »\nCounty Commissioners\n2026 Minute Archive\n2025 Minute Archive\n2024 Minute Archive\nOlder Minute Archive\nEmployment (2)\nQuick Links\nFall River Co.\nAuditors & Welfare Office\nElection Information\nElection Information\nVoter Registration\nMill Levy Sheets\nMill Levy 2021 (taxes payable in 2022)\nMill Levy 2022 (taxes payable in 2023)\nMill Levy 2023 (taxes payable in 2024)\nMill Levy 2024 (taxes payable in 2025)\nMill Levy 2025 (taxes payable in 2026)\nMill Levy by entity 2022-2026\nAudit Report\nOffice hours for the Auditor’s Office in Hot Springs are 8:00 am to 5:00 pm, M-F\nMission\nThe Auditor’s Office is responsible for auditing all accounts and maintaining all financial records in and for the county. This includes processing payroll, preparing the annual budget, establishing levies and apportioning of all tax collections. Monthly audits of all cash and cash items in the hands of the county treasurer and a verification of bank account balances are performed. Annual Financial Reports are prepared indicating the receipts and expenditures, liabilities and equity, and assets of the county.\nThe Auditor is the clerk for the Board of County Commissioners and keeps an accurate record of their official proceedings including the Board of Equalization hearings. The Auditor preserves all documents, books, and records as required by law.\nThe Auditor performs all the duties required by law relative to all county, state and federal elections held in the county. The Auditor also maintains all records of voter registration and election history.\nContact Information\nAuditor’s Office\n906 N. River St.\nHot Springs, SD 57747\n(605) 745-5130\nauditor@oglalalakotacountysd.gov\nsue.ganje@state.sd.us\nCounty Auditor: Sue Ganje sue.ganje@state.sd.us\nDeputy Auditor: Stacy Schmidt bookkeeping@oglalalakotacountysd.gov\nAdministrative Assistant : Teri Seamark agenda@oglalalakotacountysd.gov\nPayroll / Accounts Payable: Bobbie Janis payroll@oglalalakotacountysd.gov/billing@oglalalakotacountysd.gov\nElections: Arrow Bettelyoun election@oglalalakotacountysd.gov\nQuick Links\nAuditors & Welfare Office\nAbsentee Voting\nElections\nVoter Registration\nVoter Identification\nSD State Election Resources\nSD State Voter Portal\n2026 Summer Reassessment\nNational Active Fires Map\nWebsite Survey\nWebsite Survey\nPlease let us know about your visit to our site.\nWhere did you hear about this website? * Search Engine Friend Other\nWhat were your reasons for looking at our site? *\nGeneral Information\nSpecific Information\nCuriosity\nOther\nDid you find what you were looking for? *\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nIf no, what information were you looking for? (Please be specific so that we can improve our website.) *\nIf you would like a response to your request for additional information please list your email below.\nSubmit\nReturn to top of page\nCopyright © 2026 on Genesis Framework · WordPress · Log in\nNotifications",
